  "body": "Found in the two safety reads of PR #3263 (comments 7071252890 and 7071263058). This behaviour is older than that PR.\n\n`has()` in `assets/posts/wire-iso.cps` uses the JS `isFinite`, which converts its argument first. A hand-written stream with `PARAM WireU \"\"` posts `U0.`, `true` posts `U1.`, and `0x1A` posts `U26.`. The app never writes such values. The stream parser turns each real number into a number, so a text value for a wire parameter is always bad.\n\nExpected: for the wire parameters, check `typeof value !== \"number\" || !isFinite(value)` and refuse the value by name. Add a test for each of the three examples.\n\nAlso: a null `WireTaper` on an angle-word machine gives a second message, \"an angle-word taper needs one stated angle\". Remove that second message when the first refusal already names the cause. The new test of PR #3263 does not cover a bad `WirePlane` or a good section after a refused one. Add those two cases.\n",
